<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Zayd (Almohad governor of Valencia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1265</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Zayd was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> prince, a descendant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-mumin">Abd al-Mu'min</a>, and the last Almohad governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>. In 1229 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayyan-ibn-mardanish">Zayyan ibn Mardanish</a> overthrew him, and he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>, became his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and later converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, aiding the Aragonese campaigns against Valencia. He received lands in Aragon, where he died.</p></div>
